course: dictionary
lesson: 4952
title: A sudden urge: the word impulse
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An impulse is a sudden wish to do something before you have had time to think. «Buying things on impulse often means having no money for the things you really want.» The words on impulse are the clue: the buying happened quickly, without a plan.
explain: Context helps you find the meaning. «Shopping hungry leads to impulse buys, which are sudden wishes to buy.» The sentence tells you straight away that an impulse buy is a purchase made on a sudden wish. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a sudden wish to buy" fits, so you are right.
explain: Impulse can also mean other things. In science, a nerve impulse is a signal that travels along a nerve, carrying messages from the brain. Always check the words around it: is the sentence about wishes, nerves or pushes?
fact: Impulse means a sudden wish to do something without thinking about it first.
fact: In science, an impulse can be a signal that travels along a nerve, or a short push or burst of force.
fact: To act on impulse means to do something quickly, without planning it.
fact: To resist the impulse means to stop yourself from doing something you suddenly want to do.
fact: An impulse buy is something you buy on a sudden wish, not from a plan.
exercise: «Buying things on impulse often means having no money for the things you really want.» What does on impulse mean? | Slowly, after a long think | On the first day of the month | With a friend who knows the shop | *Suddenly, without planning it first
exercise: «Shopping hungry» led to a shop costing £90 instead of £70. How much extra was spent? | *£20 | £30 | £160 | £10
exercise: Which phrase means stopping yourself from doing something you suddenly want to do? | *resist the impulse | on impulse | nerve impulse | impulse buy
test: Ella says a nerve impulse is a sudden wish to buy a toy. What is the mistake? | *She mixes up the meanings: a nerve impulse is a signal along a nerve | A nerve impulse is a wish to eat | Nothing, she is right | A nerve impulse is a kind of toy
test: «The ball moved with a sudden impulse as he kicked it.» What does impulse most likely mean here? | A wish to eat | A sad feeling | A long, slow walk | *A short push, a burst of force
exam: Yasmin says, «I felt an impulse to buy the game, but I waited a day.» What does waiting show? | She bought the game at once | Impulse is a kind of game | *She practised a pause and resisted the sudden urge | She lost her money
